Summary: Keep wow64 TEBs and the PEB just under 2G, as Windows 7 does (Armadillo DRM)
Category: cpu
Kind: fix
Origin: wine-mac-builds
  Version: 11.22
  Changes: 11.21 still sets a 4G low limit for 64-bit processes with ASLR
    in the same two places; the helper returns it too
Upstream: candidate (draft in .local/bug-reports/; the placement changed
 in Wine 11.18, f0bd9046, and master is unchanged, checked 2026-11-25)
Why: Wine 11.18 (upstream f0bd9046, "Allocate initial TEB and process
 parameters in high memory on 64-bit") stopped reserving the TEB block
 top-down. In wow64 that moved the 32-bit TEBs and the PEB from just under
 2G to the bottom of the address space, next to the main stack. Armadillo,
 the DRM in Big Fish games, then fails to unpack in its child process
 ("General extraction error", hidden behind the activator), so games can't
 be activated. 10.0 and 11.0-11.17 put them high, as Windows 7's wow64
 does. In wow64 only, reserve TEB blocks top-down below 2G again; 64-bit
 processes keep upstream's placement. Big Fish's gmActivator, in a fresh
 prefix, shows the error and writes no licence on macfixes 11.22 and
 writes it on 10.0; its child makes the same calls on both up to the
 unpack. Either moving the TEB block high or not reserving the DOS area
 (both put the TEB and PEB at 0x7ffdx000) fixes it on 11.22, with the
 stack still low in both.
Programs: Big Fish games (Armadillo DRM), White Wolf and Waverly Academy
 among them: activation fails with "General extraction error" on Wine 11.18
 and later
Uncertain: why the address matters to Armadillo. Windows 7 has the TEB and
 PEB just under 2G; later Windows versions place them lower (not
 checked), yet Armadillo works there. Two changes that both put
 them at 0x7ffdx000 fix it on Wine; the main stack stays low in both.
Status: 11.21: 2026-11-16: built in wine-macfixes-11.21-build4; the
 activator writes its licence (4 values) in a fresh prefix, with no error
 box.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index 46e761e..ee83fc9 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -3718,6 +3718,27 @@ struct thread_data *virtual_alloc_first_thread_data(void)
 }
 
 
+/***********************************************************************
+ *           get_teb_block_placement
+ *
+ * In wow64, reserve TEB blocks top-down below 2G, where Wine 11.17 and
+ * earlier put them (Windows 7's wow64 has them there too). Bottom-up, the
+ * 32-bit TEB and PEB land in low memory next to the stack, and Armadillo's
+ * unpacker then fails with "General extraction error".
+ */
+static unsigned int get_teb_block_placement( ULONG_PTR *limit_low, ULONG_PTR *limit_high )
+{
+    *limit_low = *limit_high = 0;
+    if (user_space_wow_limit)
+    {
+        *limit_high = min( user_space_wow_limit, limit_2g - 1 ) & ~granularity_mask;
+        return MEM_TOP_DOWN;
+    }
+    if (use_aslr()) *limit_low = limit_4g;
+    return 0;
+}
+
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *           virtual_alloc_first_teb
  */
@@ -3727,7 +3748,8 @@ void virtual_alloc_first_teb(void)
     unsigned int status;
     struct file_view *view;
     struct thread_data *data = get_thread_data();
-    ULONG_PTR limit_low = 0, limit_high = 0;
+    ULONG_PTR limit_low, limit_high;
+    unsigned int alloc_type;
 
     set_large_address_space();
 
@@ -3735,10 +3757,8 @@ void virtual_alloc_first_teb(void)
     if (is_wow64()) teb_block_size += ROUND_SIZE( 0, sizeof(WOW_TEB), page_mask );
     teb_block_size += page_size;  /* for debug info */
 
-    if (user_space_wow_limit) limit_high = user_space_wow_limit & ~granularity_mask;
-    else if (use_aslr()) limit_low = limit_4g;
-
-    status = map_view( &view, NULL, 16 * teb_block_size, 0,
+    alloc_type = get_teb_block_placement( &limit_low, &limit_high );
+    status = map_view( &view, NULL, 16 * teb_block_size, alloc_type,
                        VPROT_READ | VPROT_WRITE, limit_low, limit_high, 0 );
     assert( !status );
     teb_block = view->base;
@@ -3784,12 +3804,10 @@ NTSTATUS virtual_alloc_teb( struct thread_data *data )
         if (!teb_block_pos)
         {
             struct file_view *view;
-            ULONG_PTR limit_low = 0, limit_high = 0;
-
-            if (user_space_wow_limit) limit_high = user_space_wow_limit & ~granularity_mask;
-            else if (use_aslr()) limit_low = limit_4g;
+            ULONG_PTR limit_low, limit_high;
+            unsigned int alloc_type = get_teb_block_placement( &limit_low, &limit_high );
 
-            if ((status = map_view( &view, NULL, 32 * teb_block_size, 0,
+            if ((status = map_view( &view, NULL, 32 * teb_block_size, alloc_type,
                                     VPROT_READ | VPROT_WRITE, limit_low, limit_high, 0 )))
             {
                 server_leave_uninterrupted_section( &virtual_mutex, &sigset );
